---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';

const seo = {
  title: 'Roatán Capital Gains Tax & ZOLITUR – Seller\'s Guide | The Agency Roatán',
  description: 'Every Bay Islands property sale pays a 4% capital gains tax to ZOLITUR — on the gain, not the price. Here\'s exactly how it works, what it costs, and when funds are released.',
};

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'Capital Gains Tax & ZOLITUR in Roatán',
  description: seo.description,
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Tomas Figueroa' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'The Agency Roatán' },
  about: { '@type': 'Thing', name: 'Real Estate Capital Gains Tax, Roatán, Honduras' },
  dateModified: '2026-09-23',
};
---

<Base title={seo.title} description={seo.description} schema={schema}>

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Seller's Guide</p>
      <h1>Capital Gains Tax &amp; ZOLITUR in Roatán</h1>
      <p class="hero-intro">
        Every property sale in the Bay Islands triggers a 4% capital gains tax paid to ZOLITUR —
        the Zone of Tourism and Free Trade. Here's how it works, how the gain is calculated,
        and what to expect at closing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-section">
    <div class="container guide-body prose">

      <h2>What is ZOLITUR?</h2>
      <p>
        ZOLITUR (Zona Libre de Turismo) is the Bay Islands' free-trade and tourism zone authority,
        established under Decreto 181-2006. Among its functions, it administers the capital gains
        tax on every real estate sale in the Bay Islands — Roatán, Utila, and Guanaja.
      </p>
      <p>
        The capital gains tax is not a title transfer tax. It's a tax on the profit you made on
        the sale, and it is separate from the 1.5% transfer tax, legal fees, and commission.
      </p>

      <div class="callout">
        <p class="callout-stat">4%</p>
        <p class="callout-label">Bay Islands capital gains rate — applied to the net gain, not the sale price</p>
        <p class="callout-note">The mainland Honduras rate is 10%. The reduced Bay Islands rate is set by Decreto 181-2006, Art. 43.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>How the gain is calculated</h2>
      <p>
        ZOLITUR taxes the <strong>net gain</strong> — what's left after deducting your cost basis
        and the agent commission from the selling price. The formula:
      </p>

      <div class="formula-block">
        <div class="formula-line">
          <span class="formula-label">Selling price</span>
          <span class="formula-value">$X</span>
        </div>
        <div class="formula-line deduct">
          <span class="formula-label">− Agent commission</span>
          <span class="formula-value">e.g. 6–8%</span>
        </div>
        <div class="formula-line deduct">
          <span class="formula-label">− Cost basis (land + improvements + acquisition costs)</span>
          <span class="formula-value">your records</span>
        </div>
        <div class="formula-line total">
          <span class="formula-label">= Taxable gain</span>
          <span class="formula-value">× 4%</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>
        Your cost basis is the price you originally paid for the property, plus documented
        improvements and acquisition costs (legal fees, stamps, surveys). Good records lower
        your tax. If you have no documentation, ZOLITUR may use the registered deed value as
        the basis, which could be lower than what you actually paid.
      </p>

      <h2>What it costs in practice</h2>
      <p>
        Two line items appear on closing statements for capital gains:
      </p>

      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Item</th>
            <th>Amount</th>
            <th>Basis</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Capital gains tax (ZOLITUR)</td>
            <td>4%</td>
            <td>Net gain (selling price − commission − cost basis)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>CG processing + SAR declaration</td>
            <td>~$350 flat</td>
            <td>Administrative fee, paid regardless of gain size</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>
        The ~$350 processing fee covers the ZOLITUR filing and the SAR (Servicio de Administración
        de Rentas) declaration. It's a flat charge that appears on every closing statement
        regardless of the size of the gain.
      </p>

      <h2>Worked examples</h2>
      <p>
        These are modeled figures, not real transactions. All prices are in USD.
      </p>

      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Scenario</th>
            <th>$270,000 sale</th>
            <th>$715,000 sale</th>
            <th>$1,200,000 sale</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Modeled cost basis</td>
            <td>$200,000</td>
            <td>$550,000</td>
            <td>$800,000</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Commission (8%)</td>
            <td>$21,600</td>
            <td>$57,200</td>
            <td>$96,000</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Taxable gain</td>
            <td>$48,400</td>
            <td>$107,800</td>
            <td>$304,000</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="highlight-row">
            <td>Capital gains tax (4%)</td>
            <td>$1,936</td>
            <td>$4,312</td>
            <td>$12,160</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Processing fee (~$350)</td>
            <td>$350</td>
            <td>$350</td>
            <td>$350</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="total-row">
            <td>Total CG costs</td>
            <td>$2,286</td>
            <td>$4,662</td>
            <td>$12,510</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p class="table-note">
        Assumptions: 8% commission, illustrative cost bases. Actual gain depends on your records.
        Consult a licensed Honduran attorney for your specific transaction.
      </p>

      <h2>When are funds released?</h2>
      <p>
        Seller proceeds are held until two things happen:
      </p>
      <ol class="guide-list">
        <li>ZOLITUR confirms the capital-gains amount — the buyer's attorney or a local accountant
            typically prepares the filing, and ZOLITUR issues a certificate once the tax is paid.</li>
        <li>The seller completes the bank's anti-money-laundering due-diligence form (SAR declaration).
            This is standard for any wire in Honduras above a threshold amount.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Both steps are routine and handled by your closing attorney. In practice, expect 2–5 business
        days for ZOLITUR to issue the certificate after payment. Build this into your expected
        closing timeline.
      </p>

      <h2>Bay Islands vs. mainland Honduras</h2>
      <p>
        The 4% Bay Islands rate is a significant advantage over mainland Honduras, which applies
        the standard income-tax rate to real estate gains — typically 10% for individuals under
        the simplified regime. The reduced rate is part of the ZOLITUR charter and applies to
        all Bay Islands municipalities.
      </p>

      <div class="compare-grid">
        <div class="compare-card">
          <p class="compare-location">Bay Islands</p>
          <p class="compare-rate">4%</p>
          <p class="compare-basis">On the net gain</p>
          <p class="compare-law">Decreto 181-2006, Art. 43</p>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-card compare-card--muted">
          <p class="compare-location">Mainland Honduras</p>
          <p class="compare-rate">10%</p>
          <p class="compare-basis">On the net gain</p>
          <p class="compare-law">Standard ISR regime</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>What sellers need to have ready</h2>
      <p>
        To keep the closing process smooth, gather these documents before listing:
      </p>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>Your original purchase deed (<em>escritura de compraventa</em>) — establishes the cost basis</li>
        <li>Receipts or invoices for any improvements made to the property</li>
        <li>Proof of acquisition costs paid at your original closing (legal fees, stamps, surveys)</li>
        <li>A valid RTN (Registro Tributario Nacional — Honduran tax ID). If you don't have one, budget ~$150 per person or ~$300 per corporation to obtain it before closing.</li>
        <li>Current property tax receipts (unpaid taxes must be cleared before the cadastral certificate issues)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If property improvements are not yet registered, a registration fee will apply at closing —
        about $600 on the transactions we've reviewed. Register improvements early to avoid delays.
      </p>

      <hr class="section-rule" />

      <div class="cta-band">
        <p class="cta-heading">Thinking of selling your Roatán property?</p>
        <p class="cta-sub">I can walk you through all of the seller costs — including capital gains — before you decide to list.</p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn-primary">Talk to Tomas</a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  /* ── Hero ── */
  .page-hero {
    padding-block: var(--space-16) var(--space-10);
    background: var(--plaster);
    border-bottom: var(--hairline);
  }

  .page-hero h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-sleek);
    font-size: clamp(var(--text-4xl), 5vw, var(--text-5xl));
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-sleek);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--iron);
    margin: var(--space-3) 0 0;
  }

  .hero-intro {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--iron-60);
    max-width: 60ch;
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  /* ── Guide body ── */
  .guide-section {
    padding-block: var(--space-16) var(--space-24);
  }

  .guide-body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-chic);
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    color: var(--iron);
    margin: var(--space-12) 0 var(--space-4);
  }

  .guide-body h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .guide-body p {
    color: var(--iron-60);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .guide-body strong {
    color: var(--iron);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* ── Callout ── */
  .callout {
    background: var(--iron);
    color: var(--canvas);
    padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-10);
    margin: var(--space-8) 0;
  }

  .callout-stat {
    font-family: var(--font-sleek);
    font-size: var(--text-7xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--agency-red);
    line-height: 1;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
  }

  .callout-label {
    font-family: var(--font-sleek);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-sleek);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--canvas);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  .callout-note {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.55);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Formula block ── */
  .formula-block {
    background: var(--plaster);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--agency-red);
    padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-8);
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .formula-line {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--iron-60);
  }

  .formula-line.deduct {
    color: var(--iron-60);
  }

  .formula-line.total {
    border-top: var(--hairline);
    padding-top: var(--space-3);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--iron);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
  }

  .formula-value {
    font-family: var(--font-sleek);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-sleek);
    color: var(--iron);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* ── Tables ── */
  .data-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .data-table th {
    font-family: var(--font-sleek);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-sleek);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--iron-40);
    text-align: left;
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--iron-20);
  }

  .data-table td {
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--iron-10);
    color: var(--iron-60);
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  .data-table td:first-child {
    color: var(--iron);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .data-table tr.highlight-row td {
    color: var(--agency-red);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .data-table tr.highlight-row td:first-child {
    color: var(--agency-red);
  }

  .data-table tr.total-row td {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--iron-20);
    border-bottom: none;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--iron);
  }

  .table-note {
    font-size: var(--text-xs) !important;
    color: var(--iron-40) !important;
    margin-top: calc(-1 * var(--space-2)) !important;
  }

  /* ── Lists ── */
  .guide-list {
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .guide-list li {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--iron-60);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  /* ── Comparison grid ── */
  .compare-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .compare-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  .compare-card {
    background: var(--iron);
    padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-8);
  }

  .compare-card--muted {
    background: var(--plaster);
  }

  .compare-location {
    font-family: var(--font-sleek);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-sleek);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.55);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
  }

  .compare-card--muted .compare-location {
    color: var(--iron-40);
  }

  .compare-rate {
    font-family: var(--font-sleek);
    font-size: var(--text-6xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--agency-red);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-1);
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .compare-card--muted .compare-rate {
    color: var(--iron-40);
  }

  .compare-basis {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.70);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
  }

  .compare-card--muted .compare-basis {
    color: var(--iron-60);
  }

  .compare-law {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.40);
    margin: 0;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .compare-card--muted .compare-law {
    color: var(--iron-40);
  }

  /* ── Divider & CTA ── */
  .section-rule {
    border: none;
    border-top: var(--hairline);
    margin: var(--space-12) 0;
  }

  .cta-band {
    background: var(--iron);
    padding: var(--space-10) var(--space-8);
  }

  .cta-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-sleek);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-sleek);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--canvas);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
  }

  .cta-sub {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.60);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
  }

  .btn-primary {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-8);
    background: var(--agency-red);
    color: var(--canvas);
    font-family: var(--font-sleek);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-sleek);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: opacity var(--duration-fast);
  }

  .btn-primary:hover {
    opacity: 0.88;
  }
</style>
